{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>With lower, second, and third decks.</b> One must wonder: if it was necessary to divide each level according to its purpose — the upper for man, the middle for dwelling, the lower for refuse — then why did He not command to make them as a single flat expanse? And why were they made one atop the other specifically? And this hints that these three levels were fashioned in semblance to the three worlds themselves, for at the time of the Flood all the worlds were disrupted and the constellations did not function at all; therefore the ark was made in this design to indicate their continued existence. And what is written, ״וְאֶל אַמָּה תְּכַלֶּנָּה מִלְמַעְלָה״ (Genesis 6:16) — according to this, the roof above was only the width of one cubit, and beneath it two cubits, widening continually like every thing that flows and expands. This hints that He, blessed be He, alone is one in the uttermost degree of unity, and whatever is closer and closer to the First Cause, blessed be He, is found to have a greater share in the matter of unity. For the angels that are near Him, blessed be He — even though there is among them a multiplicity of species, for this one was created from fire and this one from water and this one from winds — nevertheless they do not contain a compound of four elements; rather, each one of them is from a single simple element without compounding. And the middle world — in addition to the multiplicity of species — each one of them contains a compound of two elements, for the heavens were created from fire and from water. Beneath them, the lower ones, which contain a compound of four elements. If so, the entire structure flows and widens upward until it stands at the top upon one cubit, indicating that He, blessed be He, rides upon these three worlds — lower, second, and third. And this design was given to Noah to indicate that all the worlds would return to their former state in the merit of ״צַדִּיק יְסוֹד עוֹלָם״ (Proverbs 10:25)."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:27:24.225897932Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}